# React Native Platform & Runtime

The mobile environment is hostile: backgrounding, low memory, flaky networks,
keyboards, gestures. Code defensively for it.

## Storage

- Use **MMKV** (`react-native-mmkv`) over `AsyncStorage`. Synchronous, ~30x
  faster, native-backed.
- Auth tokens go in `expo-secure-store` (Keychain / Keystore), NEVER MMKV
  or AsyncStorage. See `00-core-principles.mdc`.
- All storage access goes through `@/services/storage` — never call MMKV
  directly from a screen or hook.

## App lifecycle

- Handle background ↔ foreground correctly via `AppState`.
  - Pause expensive work (timers, polling, animations) on `background`.
  - Re-derive time-sensitive state on `active` (don't decrement during
    background — recompute from absolute timestamps).
  - Refetch stale server state on resume (TanStack Query's `focusManager`
    handles this when bound to AppState — keep it bound).

## Keyboard-safe layouts

- Every screen with an input MUST handle the soft keyboard.
- Use `KeyboardAvoidingView` with `behavior="padding"` on iOS and
  `behavior="height"` on Android (when `edgeToEdgeEnabled: true`, only
  `height` reliably shrinks the layout).
- Pin the primary CTA above the keyboard — never let it scroll out of view.
  Wrap content in a `ScrollView` with `keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"`.

## Network resilience

- Support flaky networks. Subscribe to `@react-native-community/netinfo` at
  the screen level for any submit-style action; disable submit while offline,
  re-enable on reconnect.
- Bind TanStack Query's `onlineManager` to NetInfo — already done in
  `src/api/onlineManager.ts`. Keep it that way.
- All requests have an `AbortController` and a 10–15s timeout. Cancel
  in-flight requests on screen unmount.
- Treat 5xx as ambiguous — the side effect MIGHT have happened. Surface to
  the user; don't silently retry side-effecting writes.

## Providers & Context

- Avoid excessive Context providers. Each provider re-renders its entire
  subtree on change. If a value changes often, lift it OUT of Context and
  put it in Zustand with selectors.
- The provider stack in `_layout.tsx` is a budget — keep it under 6 layers.

## Loading & feedback

- Use skeleton loaders for content that has a known shape; spinners only for
  ambiguous waits (< 1s expected). Skeletons read as "this is what's coming"
  — spinners read as "something is broken".

## Testing matrix

- Test on a low-memory Android device (≤ 2GB RAM) before shipping.
- Test on iOS smallest supported screen + Android smallest supported screen.
- Test with airplane mode toggled mid-flow.
- Test backgrounding mid-request, mid-OTP, mid-form.
